             -----------Docs for NastyWall---------------
I'm a bit sick of the wall programs on boards at the mo they all seem to look
and act the same way.  So I have added a few changes to Nastywall.

 I have tried to gain interest in using the program you have all logged onto
a BBs and been prompted to scribble something on a wall if the wall program
looks messy and boring chances are your not gonna bother to write on it.
This is where NastyWall comes in its different and so make the users
interested in it.

ALL users on G.B.H.  have studied it and most have scribbled on it where as
before with a standard wall installed noone but the LoONs were using it, All
LoONs use the wall to slag each other off, our way of having a bit of a
laugh.

Most hated walls have 1 or more of the following.
1 - BackDoors (Why be a 16 sandwich eating fat fucking LAMER)
2 - Random Colours for the text (VERY VERY scruffy)
3 - BBS Plugs Before or After the Wall has shown (LAME)
4 - NO Bricks. (Shit that wouldn't hold the house up)

As I believe in user editability this wall will remain in Arexx format, it
will have to anyway as I know nowt about C or ASM, if anyone wants to write
this wall in C and send it to me along witha C compiler I would be very
interested in learning it.  Arexx may be a little slow but at least even the
stupidest sysop can check for backdoors.

You can now use Number characters on the wall (0-9) in the previous version I
decided that all (0-9) characters were a possible BBS PLUG and redirected
from the wall to a definable BBS Adder.  This can still be done in this
version but you get asked this time.

All files needed are in the archive for this.  install it like any other
AREXX door if you cant do that then get out of the BBS game as its lamers
like you that give us a BAD name.

Editable option in the Arexx program.

Nastypath="DOORS:Arexx/"   <-Set this to the path you install Wall into
RXCommand="SYS:RexxC/Rx"   <-where dos can find RX
BBSPLUG="BBS Lister/Adder" <-The name of the BBS lister/adder
BBSACC=200                 <-Access level needed to use BBS lister/adder
BBSREXX="DOORS:ADDBBS/Addbbstologoff.Rexx" <location of BBSAdder

VN_Wall.hdr <-this is for you to add your Brick effects or anything else you
              may want to put in before the main wall is displayed.

Format of VN_Hdr=21 Lines 80 Columns.
